      "updated": 1787611723761,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Kernel Mechanics & Process Isolation",
      "fontSize": 8.481112360936464,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Kernel Mechanics & Process Isolation",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "V8czyV3RbEGwzcKc-wY8-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 197.93223618286717,
      "y": 518.2751706714789,
      "width": 365.3126043818421,
      "height": 127.21668541404695,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1021487841,
      "version": 716,
      "versionNonce": 1438426689,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787611723761,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🐧 Kernel Mechanics & Process Isolation: How namespaces, cgroups, and root\nfilesystems isolate processes, alongside how PID 1 handles signals like\nSIGTERM 🛑 and prevents zombie processes.\n\n📦 Image Architecture & Container Hardening: Writing minimal custom\nDockerfiles from scratch (Debian/Alpine), running processes in the foreground\nwithout process managers, managing secrets securely 🔐, and enforcing non-root\nexecution.\n\n🌐 Service Orchestration & Networking: Designing deterministic docker-compose\ntopologies, internal DNS discovery across isolated bridge networks 🔌, and\nresilient volume mounts 💾 for persistent data.",
      "fontSize": 8.481112360936462,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🐧 Kernel Mechanics & Process Isolation: How namespaces, cgroups, and root filesystems isolate processes, alongside how PID 1 handles signals like SIGTERM 🛑 and prevents zombie processes.\n\n📦 Image Architecture & Container Hardening: Writing minimal custom Dockerfiles from scratch (Debian/Alpine), running processes in the foreground without process managers, managing secrets securely 🔐, and enforcing non-root execution.\n\n🌐 Service Orchestration & Networking: Designing deterministic docker-compose topologies, internal DNS discovery across isolated bridge networks 🔌, and resilient volume mounts 💾 for persistent data.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
